---
name: Reduce HarfangLab OCSF events for a SIEM
description: |
  Drains the Splunk pull export of a HarfangLab Manager every minute, keeps
  every OCSF event in ClickHouse as the data lake, and sends Splunk a reduced
  stream: network and HTTP activity become summaries, process starts and
  module loads pass through once with their repeats summarized, and all other
  events pass through unchanged.

  Splunk indexes each event at its event time, which HarfangLab gives in
  epoch milliseconds, with a sourcetype per OCSF class, such as
  `harfanglab:ocsf:network_activity`. Summaries arrive up to one window after
  the events that they count, so searches over them should select by index
  time (`_index_earliest`). Create the ClickHouse table before you start the
  pipeline, for example with a `JSON` catch-all column.
---

every 1min {
  harfanglab::fetch "https://example.hurukai.io:8443",
    token=secret("harfanglab-api-token")
}
fork {
  harfanglab::ocsf::reduce
  to_splunk "https://splunk.example.com:8088",
    hec_token=secret("splunk-hec-token"),
    time=from_epoch(time * 1ms),
    sourcetype=("harfanglab:ocsf:"
      + ocsf_class_name(class_uid).to_lower().replace(" ", "_"))
}
to_clickhouse host="clickhouse.example.com", table="harfanglab_ocsf",
  mode="append"
